# The topmost certificate of the chain each host sent, recorded on 2026-09-29 with
#     openssl s_client -connect <host>:443 -servername <host> -showcerts
# and reduced the way ESP-IDF v5.3's esp_crt_verify_callback sees it: follow the sent
# certificates from the leaf to its issuer while one is there and its signature checks; the
# last one reached is the top, and the bundle is searched for the top's issuer. Hosts that
# send the same top share one entry.
#
# `needs-anchor` entries fail with cacert.pem alone and pass with anchors.pem; `store`
# entries pass with cacert.pem alone. test_ca_store.py checks both, and fails when an anchor
# in software/wifi/ca_store/anchors.pem is needed by no entry here that has not expired.
# Re-record when a host changes its chain, and remove an entry when no host sends it.

